A||||10||fiero56||plug wires||||5||
Z||000000||fiero56||10-18-2000||12:07 AM||||I was helping WT III with his project car this evening, and when I was getting ready to leave, letting the engine warm for a minute, I popped the decklid, just to look around in there after dark. First thing we noticed was that my spark plug wires are arcing pretty badly. They arc from the coil, to the block, across each other, etc. They are 7mm AutoZone $15 specials with about a year of wear and tear on them. I had a very expensive set on previously, but they burned up from exhaust heat, and I went cheap instead. My question is what plug wires have others used with good results. Price is not really a factor, but something reasonably priced would be nice. Any suggestions?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pffsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Seanh||10-18-2000||12:52 AM||||I have been running Accel's 8.8mm Race Wires from Advanced Auto for about 6 months. I really like them and havent have any trouble with them yet.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||10-18-2000||11:33 AM||||I've had a set of FOCOA red wires on my 87 for a couple of years.<P>I had some GM replacement wires on my 88 for 6 months before the heat got to them from the 3.1 I was running.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||10-18-2000||11:38 AM||||I use the Accel 8.8mm wires. I've had them for 3 years without any problems.||||reg||1
Z||000004||PatrickB||10-18-2000||11:46 AM||||Im using the MSD Heli-Core's and have been satisified with them.  They have a fit for the fiero so you dont have to cut them and nice big, thick boots.  I dont have to use those metal ones anymore.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||10-18-2000||11:55 AM||||My first thought was Accel wires, but WT III doesn't seem to think they are very good. I will still look into them, but the MSDs sound most appealing right now. Where did you get them?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Carrolles||10-18-2000||12:12 PM||||I've been running the FOCOA red wires for about a year now.  So far so good.||||reg||1
Z||000007||StuGood||10-18-2000||12:39 PM||||I have used "Koolwire" plug wire sets from (I think) Pep Boys.  They are reasonably priced, are precut and assembled, and have lasted for quite a few years without giving any problems.<P>Of course, when I install them, I take care to route them carefully and keep them loomed and tied off, away from the exhaust manifolds, sharp edges, and so forth.<P>Proper installation is the key.  Last time, I replaced a very pretty set of yellow Accel silicon (8mm?)wires on an old used car, with plain old grey Koolwires.  Reason?  One of the fancy yellow wires was melted, like a fried egg, to one of the mainfolds.  Needless to say, it ran <B>much</B> better afterwards  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">!<P>A couple other things to note:  I believe the  boots (plug ends) are supposed to have metal heat shields on them, to protect the boots from exhaust manifold heat.  Replace them if they are missing.  Also, if you have exhaust manifold leak(s), the heat could damage the plug boots in short order.       <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 10-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Alex4mula||10-18-2000||12:58 PM||||I have used the Accel 8.8 and Jacobs. For the price & performance I recommend the Jacobs wires by far. They have a set to Fit the V6. Also they have a lifetime warranty. If they arc, break or burn Jacobs will replace them free. I have tried their warranty and works. Just make sure you store the original receipt very well. Cost me $66. I recommend buying them directly from Jacobs Electronics. Also heard good things about Nology & MSD.||||reg||1
Z||000009||WisconsinGT||10-18-2000||02:11 PM||||I have been using Splitfires for 8months. No problems here. I think they are great if you can get past the blue color.||||reg||1
Z||000010||kslish||10-18-2000||02:40 PM||||Magnecor 8.5mm Race Wires (www.magnecor.com)<P>Check out their web page, lots of info.  Used by a lot of Nascar and NHRA teams.<P>They are red just like the stock wires and are the best wires I have ever seen.<P>Not cheap though......best price available for the Fiero V6 is $75.99 at Cyberauto (www.cyberauto.com).<P>||||reg||14
